# A filter must move below a sort, since a sort never changes values or rows.

admin 'create table test::t19 { id: int4, a: int4 }'
---
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |   id    |  namespace  |  table  |  created  |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |  16388  |    test     |   t19   |   true    |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
>

query 'CALL rql::explain("from test::t19 sort {id:asc} filter {a > 1}")'
---
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+---------------------+
> |  idx  |  depth  |  parent  |    kind     |       detail        |
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+---------------------+
> |   0   |    0    |   none   |    Sort     |       id ASC        |
> |   1   |    1    |    0     |   Filter    |  (a > Constant(1))  |
> |   2   |    2    |    1     |  TableScan  |      test::t19      |
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+---------------------+
>
